>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `CLARIFY_STEP_TAC`

``` hol4
classicalLib.CLARIFY_STEP_TAC : thm list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Performs one non-branching safe classical-reasoning step.

`CLARIFY_STEP_TAC thms` tries the clarification cascade once. Its base
cascade accepts built-in safe steps, safe rules with at most one premise, and
two-premise safe rules when one child closes immediately by assumption or
contradiction. It rejects rules with three or more premises and genuinely
branching two-premise rules, and it does not perform assumption modus ponens.
Registered safe wrappers also participate. The tactic may solve the goal or
return one residual goal.

The theorem list accepts `SIntro`, `Intro`, `SElim`, `Elim`, `SDest`, `Dest`
and `Del` markers, locally for this invocation. Every unmarked theorem is
inserted as an assumption before the step is attempted. Content-bearing
generic simplifier wrappers are unwrapped and inserted; inert generic
controls are ignored.

Unlike `CLARIFY_TAC`, this tactic does not repeat the cascade.

### Failure

Fails if no clarification step applies. In particular, it fails when the
only available safe step would leave two genuinely open branches. Malformed
extra rules can also cause failure while the theorem list is processed.

### Example

On the goal `p ==> p`, one invocation introduces the antecedent and leaves
`{p} ?- p`. Repeated clarification, as performed by `CLARIFY_TAC []`, then
closes the goal.

``` hol4
classicalLib.CLARIFY_STEP_TAC []
```

